nod|n|Inlay; inlaid or mosaic work; something ornamental inserted in a surface. ; A visible sign of an idea; an object, or the figure of an object, symbolizing and suggesting another object, or an idea, by natural aptness or by association; a figurative representation; a typical designation; a symbol; as, a balance is an emblem of justice; a scepter, the emblem of sovereignty or power; a circle, the emblem of eternity. ; A picture accompanied with a motto, a set of verse, or the like, intended as a moral lesson or meditation.	a:ruy,61,2;vs8,60,3;hda,52,4;28d8,40,1;1cdz,9,2~hda,52,4;vs8,60,3;ruy,61,2;1cdz,9,2;28d8,40,1	v:1tuh,16,2~1tuh,16,2	n:ruy,75,5;1bic,57,5;sjp,31,3;1tuh,6,1~ruy,75,5;1bic,57,5;sjp,31,3;1tuh,6,1	N:xms,116,7~xms,116,7
